  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Now that you know what a queue is, let's look at&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">where and how it actually gets used</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;both in real systems and in coding problems.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-where-queues-show-up-in-real-life",
      "title": "1. Where Queues Show Up in Real Life",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every time you see things being processed&nbsp;<strong>in order</strong>, there is likely a queue behind it.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "items": [],
          "url": "",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "{\"headers\":[\"Scenario\",\"How queue is used\"],\"rows\":[[\"WhatsApp messages\",\"delivered in the order sent\"],[\"YouTube video buffering\",\"chunks loaded and played in order\"],[\"Uber ride requests\",\"drivers assigned in order of request\"],[\"Food delivery apps\",\"orders queued and dispatched in order\"],[\"Bank transactions\",\"processed one by one in order received\"]]}",
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<hr style=\"border-width: 1px medium medium; border-style: solid none none; border-color: rgb(224, 224, 224) currentcolor currentcolor; border-image: none; margin: 24px 0px;\">",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-where-queues-show-up-in-code",
      "title": "2. Where Queues Show Up in Code",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Queues are widely used in programming whenever tasks or data need to be processed&nbsp;<strong>in order or level by level</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "They help manage flow efficiently in algorithms like traversal, scheduling, and real-time processing.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "1. Breadth First Search (BFS)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The most classic use of a queue in interviews. BFS explores a graph or tree&nbsp;<strong>level by level</strong>&nbsp;and a queue is what makes that possible.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116777-72712884.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116777-72712884.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116777-72712884.png",
          "alt": "Breadth First Search BFS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 1:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Start by enqueueing the root node</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">1</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">. Queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[1]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 2:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">1</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it, and enqueue its children</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">2 and 3</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">. Queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[2, 3]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 3:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">2</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it, and enqueue its children</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">4 and 5</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">. Queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[3, 4, 5]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 4:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">3</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it, and enqueue its children</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">6 and 7</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">. Queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[4, 5, 6, 7]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">S</strong><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">tep 5:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">4</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it. It has no children, so queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[5, 6, 7]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 6:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">5</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it. It has no children, so queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[6, 7]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 7:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">6</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it. It has no children, so queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[7]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 8:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Dequeue</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">7</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, visit it. Queue becomes</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">(empty), so BFS ends.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<i><strong>BFS uses a queue (FIFO):</strong>Nodes are visited level by level, starting from the root →&nbsp;<strong>1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7</strong>.</i>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<i>At each step, you&nbsp;<strong>dequeue a node and enqueue its children</strong>, which ensures all nodes at the current level are processed before moving deeper.</i>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<i>The process continues until the&nbsp;<strong>queue becomes empty</strong>, meaning all nodes have been visited.</i>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();\nq.offer(root);\n\nwhile (!q.isEmpty()) {\n    int node = q.poll();          // process front\n    q.offer(node.left);           // enqueue left child\n    q.offer(node.right);          // enqueue right child\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "2. Level Order Traversal",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Level Order Traversal",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "&nbsp;is just&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "BFS applied to a tree",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", where nodes are visited&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "level by level from top to bottom",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ".",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116777-891264743.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\"></span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Level 0:</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;Start with the root →&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">1</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Level 1:</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;Visit children of 1 →&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">2, 3</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Level 2:</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;Visit children of 2 and 3 →&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">4, 5, 6, 7</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The trick check the&nbsp;<strong>queue size at the start of each level</strong>. That tells you exactly how many nodes belong to the current level.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n    int levelSize = q.size();          // nodes in this level\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {\n        int node = q.poll();\n        // process node\n        // enqueue its children\n    }\n    // one full level done\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "3. Sliding Window Using Deque",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For each window of size&nbsp;<strong>K = 3</strong>, we look at the elements inside the window and find the&nbsp;<strong>maximum value</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 1:&nbsp;</strong>Window<strong>[3, 1, 5]&nbsp;</strong>→ maximum is&nbsp;<strong>5</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116778-432008695.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 2:&nbsp;</strong>Slide window →<strong>[1, 5, 2]</strong>→ maximum is&nbsp;<strong>5</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116778-806640538.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 3:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Slide again →</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[5, 2, 4]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">→ maximum is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">5</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116778-189178415.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\"></span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Final output:&nbsp;<strong>[5, 5, 5]</strong>, as each window’s maximum is recorded while sliding from left to right.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A deque keeps track of&nbsp;<strong>useful elements only&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;elements that can never be the maximum are thrown out immediately.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "Deque<Integer> dq = new ArrayDeque<>();\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\n    // remove elements outside the window\n    if (!dq.isEmpty() && dq.peekFirst() < i - k + 1)\n        dq.pollFirst();\n\n    // remove smaller elements from back — they are useless\n    while (!dq.isEmpty() && arr[dq.peekLast()] < arr[i])\n        dq.pollLast();\n\n    dq.offerLast(i);\n\n    if (i >= k - 1)\n        result.add(arr[dq.peekFirst()]);   // front is always max\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "4.Task Scheduling",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In&nbsp;<strong>task scheduling</strong>, a queue ensures tasks are handled in<strong>FIFO order</strong>, so the task that arrives first (<strong>T1</strong>) is processed first.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116778-437540836.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Once&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">T1</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">is completed, it is removed from the front, and the next task (</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">T2</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">) moves forward to be processed, followed by&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">T3</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">and</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">T4</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This approach is widely used in&nbsp;<strong>operating systems, print queues, and server request handling</strong>, where tasks must be executed&nbsp;<strong>one at a time in order</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "5.Generating Numbers in Sequence",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116949-999847382.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Start by enqueueing&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">\"1\"</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">. This is the first binary number, and the queue begins as&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">[\"1\"]</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Dequeue&nbsp;<strong>\"1\"</strong>, print it, and enqueue&nbsp;<strong>\"10\"&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong>\"11\"&nbsp;</strong>. Then dequeue&nbsp;<strong>\"10\"&nbsp;</strong>, print it, and enqueue&nbsp;<strong>\"100\"&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong>\"101\"</strong>.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next, dequeue&nbsp;<strong>\"11\"</strong>, print it, and enqueue<strong>\"110\"</strong>and<strong>\"111\"</strong>.Continue this process until you generate&nbsp;<strong>N numbers</strong>. For&nbsp;<strong>N = 6</strong>, the output becomes&nbsp;<strong>1, 10, 11, 100, 101, 110</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "Queue<String> q = new LinkedList<>();\nq.offer(\"1\");\n\nfor (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    String front = q.poll();\n    System.out.println(front);\n    q.offer(front + \"0\");\n    q.offer(front + \"1\");\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A&nbsp;<strong>queue preserves order automatically</strong>, so you don’t need sorting elements are processed exactly in the sequence they are inserted.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-recognizing-patterns-helps",
      "title": "3. Recognizing patterns helps:",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">“process in order” → use a simple queue</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">,</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">“level by level” → use BFS (queue)</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">,</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">“sliding window max/min” → use deque</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">,</span>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "<p><strong>“highest priority first” → use a priority queue</strong>.These signals quickly guide you to the&nbsp;<strong>right data structure</strong>, making problems easier and more efficient to solve.</p>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    }
